 Labor Law Art. 51 (as amended by M/44 of 1446H) with Regulation Art. 18(2) | The employment contract must be written in two copies, one kept by each party, and must be documented in accordance with the relevant statutory provisions and as the Regulation sets out; the contract exists even if unwritten, in which case the worker alone may prove it and his rights by all means of proof, and either party may demand a written contract at any time. Regulation Art. 18(2): the employer must document workers' contracts electronically through the ministry's approved platform. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic]` for Art. 51; `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` for Regulation Art. 18 
