 Art. 18 | On transfer of ownership of the establishment or change of its legal form by merger, division or otherwise, employment contracts remain in force and service is deemed continuous; for rights accrued before the change (wages, end-of-service award deemed due at the transfer date, other rights) the successor and predecessor are jointly liable. For sole proprietorships the parties may agree, with the worker's written consent, that all prior rights pass to the new owner; a worker who does not consent may end his contract and collect his dues from the predecessor | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` `[BOE — official English]` `[authority — HRSD]` 
 Art. 84 (end-of-service award, base formula) | On the end of the employment relationship the employer must pay the worker an award for his period of service computed as half a month's wage for each of the first five years and one month's wage for each of the following years; the last wage is the basis; the worker is entitled to the award for fractions of a year in proportion to the time served | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` `[BOE — official English]` 
 Art. 85 and Art. 87 (resignation fractions and exceptions) | If the relationship ends by the worker's resignation, he is entitled to one third of the award after service of not less than two consecutive years and not more than five years, two thirds if his service exceeds five consecutive years but is less than ten, and the full award if his service is ten years or more (Art. 85). By exception to Art. 85, the full award is due if the worker leaves because of force majeure beyond his control, or if a female worker ends the contract within six months of her marriage or three months of giving birth (Art. 87) | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` `[BOE — official English]` 
