| all | ZATCA — zakat / corporate income tax return | Every company and branch must file its annual zakat and/or income-tax return electronically on the ZATCA portal within 120 days of the end of its fiscal year and pay the amount due with the return; Saudi/GCC-owned shares of capital are subject to zakat (2.5% of the zakat base) and non-GCC-owned shares to corporate income tax (20% on the taxable share of profits; higher rates for oil and gas); mixed companies file one combined return. Audited financial statements must be attached where the entity is required to have them. Late filing and late payment penalties apply (filing: 5–25% of unpaid tax by delay band; payment: 1% per 30 days). A zakat/tax certificate (شهادة) is issued on filing and payment and is required for government contract payments and for closing out contracts. | (من الذاكرة، غير مقروء من نص رسمي:) تُقدم الإقرارات الزكوية والضريبية خلال (120) يومًا من نهاية السنة المالية ويُسدد المستحق معها. | Diarise FYE + 120 days (30 April for a calendar-year entity). The rates, penalty bands and certificate rules are model knowledge; obtain the Income Tax Law (Royal Decree M/1 of 1425H, as amended) and the Zakat Collection Regulations before advising on liability. Zakat-only entities do not get the Companies Law audit exemption in practice because ZATCA may require audited statements above a revenue level `[model knowledge — verify]`. | `[model knowledge — verify]` |
| all (VAT-registered) | ZATCA — VAT returns | Registration for VAT is mandatory where annual taxable supplies exceed SAR 375,000 (voluntary above SAR 187,500). VAT returns are monthly for taxpayers whose annual taxable supplies exceed SAR 40 million and quarterly for others; each return and payment is due by the last day of the month following the end of the tax period. Standard rate 15% since 1 July 2020. Late-filing penalty 5–25% of the tax due; late-payment penalty 5% per month or part. | (من الذاكرة:) تكون الفترة الضريبية شهرية لمن تتجاوز توريداته السنوية (40) مليون ريال وربع سنوية لغيرهم، ويقدم الإقرار ويسدد خلال الشهر التالي لنهاية الفترة. | The SAR 40 million monthly/quarterly split is the only turnover-dependent recurring filing in this calendar; the tracker needs the entity's latest annual taxable supplies to pick the frequency. Group registration and branch treatment are ZATCA rules not read. | `[model knowledge — verify]` |
| all | ZATCA — withholding tax | Payments by a Saudi resident (or branch) to a non-resident for services, royalties, rent, management fees, dividends, interest and similar are subject to withholding tax at 5%, 15% or 20% depending on the payment type (treaty relief available), to be withheld and paid to ZATCA with a monthly WHT return within the first 10 days of the month following payment; an annual WHT reconciliation is filed with the annual return within 120 days of year end. | (من الذاكرة:) يلتزم المقيم بحجز الضريبة عن المدفوعات لغير المقيمين وتوريدها مع إقرار شهري خلال (10) أيام من نهاية الشهر الذي تم فيه الدفع. | Monthly event whenever a payment to a non-resident is made — group management fees and royalties are the usual triggers in diligence. Rates and the 10-day deadline are from memory; the Income Tax Law Art. 68 and the Regulations were not read. | `[model knowledge — verify]` |
