| all (with related-party dealings) | ZATCA — transfer pricing | Under the Transfer Pricing Bylaws, taxpayers (income-tax payers from 2019; zakat payers from fiscal years starting 1 January 2024) must file a controlled-transactions disclosure form with the annual return, and maintain a master file and local file where related-party transactions exceed SAR 6 million in the year (with an affidavit from a licensed auditor on the disclosure form for larger taxpayers); country-by-country reporting applies to groups with consolidated revenue of SAR 3.2 billion or more, with notification by year end and the report within 12 months. | (من الذاكرة:) يُقدم نموذج الإفصاح عن المعاملات مع الأطراف ذات العلاقة مع الإقرار السنوي، ويُحتفظ بالملف الرئيس والملف المحلي إذا تجاوزت المعاملات (6) ملايين ريال. | Diarise with the FYE + 120 days return; the master/local file must exist by then even though it is filed only on request. The zakat-payer extension, the SAR 6m and SAR 3.2bn thresholds and the affidavit rule are from memory. | `[model knowledge — verify]` |
| all | Saudi Post (SPL) — National Address | Every commercial register holder must have a registered National Address (العنوان الوطني) linked to the CR and keep it current; it is the address for official notices and is renewed/confirmed annually through the SPL business portal. | (من الذاكرة:) يجب تسجيل العنوان الوطني للمنشأة وتحديثه سنويًّا. | Low-risk, but the National Address is where the CR Art. 15 suspension warning and ZATCA notices are served; a stale address is how 14-day warnings are missed. | `[model knowledge — verify]` |

