 Art. 6 | The registration application must include: (a) applicant's name, address and ID number; (b) the trade name under which the merchant will carry on the activity; (c) the merchant's legal form; (d) the amount of the merchant's capital; (e) the name of the manager(s) or board members and their powers; (f) the address of the head office; (g) other data set by the Regulation. The Regulation may require bank-account and other data after registration. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` 
 Art. 9 | A merchant may register different activities in the commercial register; homogeneity between them is not required, without prejudice to other laws. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` 
 Art. 11 | The merchant must submit annually to the Registrar a confirmation of the data recorded in the register, as set by the Regulation. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` 
 Art. 15 | Suspension: if the annual confirmation is not filed within 90 days of its due date, the Registrar suspends the registration after a 14-day warning; suspension is recorded and all licences issued on the registration are suspended. Suspension lasts one year; it is lifted on request if the merchant files the confirmation and pays the fee plus the Art. 21 fine. If not cured within the year: a merchant other than a company or foreign-company branch is deleted; a company or foreign branch may no longer apply to lift the suspension, and the Ministry may require the partners or shareholders to dissolve the company or apply to the court for dissolution. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` 
 Art. 17 | Data recorded in the register is evidence for or against the merchant from the date of recording. Data that must be recorded or updated cannot be invoked against third parties unless recorded or updated; an interested party may nevertheless invoke such data against the merchant. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` 
 Art. 20 | The competent court must notify the Registrar within 30 days of any final judgment or decision on: opening or ending bankruptcy procedures; dissolution, liquidation or nullity of companies and appointment or removal of liquidators; ending of liquidation; rehabilitation of merchants; interdiction, guardianship, agents for absentees; permission for minors to trade; criminal penalties barring the merchant from business and the appointed custodian; expulsion of partners or shareholders or removal of managers; judicial receivership and determination of heirs. The effect of such judgments is recorded on notification. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` 

codex
The Companies Law portal is responding. Its LLC provisions require a losses meeting within 60 calendar days of management learning of the threshold breach; the supplied articles also require unanimity for amendments. Low Green permits renewal of existing work permits under the reference guide, so I’m not treating it as a blanket permit block. I’m checking newer HRSD guidance before finalizing that finding.
