43:| Art. 27; Regs Arts. 12-13, 16-20 | A manager or director may not have a direct or indirect interest in the company's dealings and contracts, nor compete with the company in any branch of its activity, except with authorisation from the partners, general assembly or shareholders or their delegate; he may not exploit the company's assets, information or investment opportunities offered to him or the company. Exceptions to the interest bar: public tenders; personal-needs dealings on the company's standard terms within its ordinary activity; other cases set by the Regulations. Breach of the interest bar: the company may seek annulment and disgorgement; breach of the competition bar: damages (Art. 27). Regs Art. 12: an opportunity is off-limits if within the company's usual activities or if the company wishes or is expected to benefit from it. Regs Art. 13: a general-partnership manager needs authorisation from all partners for self-dealing (case by case) and for competing activity (renewed annually). Regs Art. 16: the general assembly may delegate the authorisation of related-party dealings to the board only where the dealing (or aggregate for the year) is below 1% of revenue per the latest financial statements and below SAR 10 million, is in the ordinary course and on non-preferential terms; delegation lasts at most one year or to the end of the board term; directors may not vote on the delegation. Regs Art. 17: indirect interest includes dealings benefiting the director's relatives, partnerships/LLCs in which he or a relative is a partner, JSCs/SJSCs in which he or relatives hold 5% or more, non-company establishments owned or managed by him or relatives, and companies where he or a relative is a manager, director or senior executive. Regs Arts. 18-19: competition authorisations may be delegated to the board with criteria, for at most one year; the director must notify the board (recorded in the minutes), abstain, and the licence is renewed annually. Regs Art. 20: if authorisation is refused the director must resign within the period set or his membership ends, unless he abandons the dealing or competition. | لا يجوز لمدير الشركة، ولا لعضو مجلس إدارتها، أن تكون له أي مصلحة مباشرة أو غير مباشرة في الأعمال والعقود التي تتم لحساب الشركة، إلا بترخيص من الشركاء أو الجمعية العامة أو المساهمين أو من يفوضونه. (اللائحة م16) أن يكون إجمالي مبلغ العمل أو العقد -أو مجموع الأعمال والعقود خلال السنة المالية- أقل من (واحد في المائة) من إيرادات الشركة وفقًا لآخر قوائم مالية، وأن يكون أقل من (عشرة) ملايين ريال سعودي. | Related-party approval is a shareholder-level matter by default; board-level approval is valid only under a delegation meeting the Regs Art. 16 thresholds. Diligence should list every contract with a director, manager, their relatives or their other companies and match each to a partners'/assembly authorisation; unauthorised contracts are voidable at the company's election with disgorgement. Non-compete undertakings by directors are statutory, not just contractual. | [settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic] [authority — MoC] |
