**Bottom line**

**🔴 8 Red · 🟡 7 Yellow · 🟢 0 Green.** The principal acquisition risks are the foreign shareholder’s operational control and 95% profit entitlement, incomplete investment authorisation, the distributor’s statutory eligibility, losses exceeding half of capital, unpaid GOSI contributions and customer termination rights. Treat resolution of the Red findings as proposed closing gates, subject to counsel’s judgment `[review]`. Missing documents prevent a clean conclusion on the remaining diligence categories.

