**Remaining diligence gaps**

Absence from these extracts is not evidence that a document does not exist or that a breach occurred.

| Category | Missing evidence and review required |
|---|---|
| Corporate records | Complete registered Arabic articles and amendments; partner resolutions and minutes; capital-payment evidence; pledges, options and side agreements; subsidiary/intercompany schedule; auditor appointment or exemption; filed financial statements; evidence of conformity with the 2022 Law. Relevant rows: `companies-law.md` Arts. 15,17–19,165,180 and Decree clause 3, `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]`. |
| CR standing | Current full CR, manager powers, annual confirmation and changes. “Active” in D§1 is a snapshot, not proof of every filing. `commercial-register-law.md` Arts. 6,11,15,17,20, `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]`. No suspension or missed deadline is established. |
| Contract completeness | Full agreements and amendments; customer identities; term, renewal, termination mechanics, MFN, exclusivity, indemnities, liability limits, guarantees and notices. No adverse finding on omitted clauses can be made. |
| Workforce liabilities | Employee-level last wages, included components, service dates, resignation/termination circumstances, accrued leave and end-of-service provisions. Under `labor-law.md` Arts. 84–87, the base award is **0.5 × W × min(S,5) + W × max(S−5,0)**, subject to applicable adjustments. `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic]` for Art. 84. **Aggregate liability: not calculable; not zero.** |
| Workforce continuity | Structure-specific analysis under `labor-law.md` Art. 18 and `platform-obligations.md` Regulation Art. 14 Second items 19–20, `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]`. Do not assume a partner change with the same CR requires worker-by-worker transfers, or that service restarts. Obtain twelve months of payroll/WPS evidence; WPS-specific practice remains `[model knowledge — verify]`. |
| Litigation and insolvency | All pending/threatened claims, regulatory inquiries, HRSD settlements, awards, reserves and Bankruptcy Register results; recent related-party payments, security and asset disposals. No claims search or clean-register conclusion is available. The `enforcement-law.md` instrument is identified in the reference set as not effective until 28 October 2026 and is not applied at this cutoff. General successor-liability doctrine: `[no rule in ksa files — verify]`. |
| IP | Founder/employee assignments, software and hardware licences, source-code rights, open-source inventory and infringement claims. No ownership chain or registry clearance is established. Saudi IP registration/recordal rules: `[no rule in ksa files — verify]`. |
| Data | Processing inventory, privacy notices, processor agreements, offshore access/hosting, transfer mechanism, processing records, breach records and assessment of DPO/DPIA triggers. Relevant rows: `personal-data-protection-law.md` Arts. 8,12,29,31 and Regulation Arts. 17,24–25,32, `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]`; transfer-mechanism details `[model knowledge — verify]`. No offshore processing or actual breach is established. |
| Government and sector contracts | Identify whether any customer falls within `government-tenders-procurement-law.md` Arts. 1/93; if so, inspect applicable assignment, subcontracting, bond, variation and penalty requirements. Sector-specific fleet/telematics authorisations require separate review where the tree lacks a rule: `[no rule in ksa files — verify]`. |
| Electronic evidence | Obtain executed versions and signature/audit records where contracts were signed electronically. Relevant rows: `electronic-transactions-law.md` Arts. 6,8–9, `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]`. No signature defect is evidenced. |

**Closing-checklist handoff — proposed items for approval**

The following is the complete inline handoff; no external checklist has been modified. Owners and closing treatment are proposed `[review]`. Authorities and tags are those stated in the linked issue numbers.

| Issues | Proposed owner | Deliverable / timing |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Target manager, Finance Lead, Saudi counsel | Evidence of the losses knowledge date and compliant assembly; approved remedial/funding plan; current solvency information before closing. Statutory meeting period: 60 calendar days from knowledge. |
| 2–3 | Both partners, corporate counsel | Required approvals, unanimity for amended articles, pre-emption notices and waivers or completed expiry process; written amendment and CR registration at completion. |
| 4,10 | Legal Lead, Saudi counsel, seller | Counsel-approved treatment of the management arrangement and historical exposure; agreed termination/replacement, accrued-fee settlement and handover of bank/operating powers. |
| 5 | Target filing officer, Legal Lead | Ownership/control reconciliation and current UBO evidence before closing; prepare transaction-driven update for filing within the applicable 15-day period after change. |
| 6 | Commercial lead, Legal Lead | Separate transaction-specific waivers from Customer 1, Customer 2 and Customer 3 before closing. Replace placeholders with verified legal names. |
| 7 | Transaction counsel | If asset transfer: assignment consents or validated advance consent and notices; appropriate release and security arrangements. |
| 8–9 | HR lead | Current Qiwa/Nitaqat and permit records, documentation of the two Saudi contracts, workforce reconciliation and agreed staffing remediation. |
| 11 | Investment adviser, Saudi counsel | Current MISA registration/update, matched activity scope, any required restricted-activity ownership approval and buyer registration. |
| 12 | Finance Lead, target payroll | Current GOSI account, payment/resolution evidence and certificate supporting completion; agreed purchase-price treatment. |
| 13 | Saudi counsel, commercial lead | Confirmed lawful distribution eligibility, registration or authorised alternative, current-term documentation and after-sales allocation. |
| 14 | Competition counsel, Finance Lead | Written three-test filing analysis; if required, notification and lawful completion clearance before implementation. |
| 15 | Accountant/tax adviser, Finance Lead | Target tax-standing pack, management-fee analysis, quantified exposures and agreed tax protections or clearance requirements. |

